          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifold"} Poisson manifold
            may be thought of as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+algebroid"} Poisson Lie algebroid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
            with extra structure: called an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-symplectic+manifold"} n-symplectic manifold
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
          %p
            By
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            this Lie algebroid should integrate to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            with extra structure. Symplectic groupoids are supposed to be those objects that integrate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-symplectic+manifold"} n-symplectic manifold
            aka
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifold"} Poisson manifold
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+algebra"} groupoid algebra
            of these symplectic groupoids are
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star+algebra"} C-star algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            of the original
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifold"} Poisson manifold
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            The original definition of
            %a{:href => "#Weinstein87"} Weinstein 1987
            is this:
          #WeinsteinsDefintion.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong symplectic Lie groupoid
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}_\bullet
              whose manifold of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}_1
              is equipped with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic structure
              whose symplectic form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi closed
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in \Omega^2_{closed}(\mathbf{X}_1)
              is
              %em multiplicative
              in that the alternating sum of its canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+a+differential+form"} pullbacks
              to the space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}_2
              of composable morphisms vanishes:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %mi δ
                    %mi ω
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi pr
                      %mn 1
                      %mo *
                    %mi ω
                    %mo −
                    %msup
                      %mi compose
                      %mo *
                    %mi ω
                    %mo +
                    %msubsup
                      %mi pr
                      %mn 2
                      %mo *
                    %mi ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 =
                    \\delta \omega = pr_1^* \omega - compose^* \omega
                    + pr_2^* \omega
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The manifold of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}_0
              of a symplectic Lie groupoid
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi X
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}_\bullet
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeinsteinsDefintion"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifold"} Poisson manifold
              which is unique, up to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \colon \mathbf{X}_1 \to \mathbf{X}_0
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifolds"} Poisson manifolds
              (canonically regarding the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{X}_1, \omega)
              as a Poisson manifold).
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifolds"} Poisson manifolds
              that arise this way as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}_0
              of a symplectic Lie groupoid are called
              = succeed "." do
                %strong integrable Poisson manifolds
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Reformulated more abstractly, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeinsteinsDefintion"}
              says that the differential form
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mn 3
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (0, \omega, 0)
                    \\in
                    \\oplus_{k = 0,1,2} \Omega^{3-k}(\mathbf{X}_{k})
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
              of degree 3 in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+de+Rham+complex"} simplicial de Rham complex
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p This observation leads to the following generalization
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong pre-quasi symplectic groupoid
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}
              equipped with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+2-form"} differential 2-form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_2 \in \Omega^2(\mathbf{X}_1)
              and a differential 3-form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_3 \in \Omega^3(\mathbf{X}_0)
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mn 3
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (0, \omega_2, \omega_3) \in \oplus_{k = 0,1,2} \Omega^{3-k}(\mathbf{X}_{k})
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+de+Rham+complex"} simplicial de Rham complex
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi X
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}_\bullet
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\delta \omega_2 = 0
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mi δ
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 3
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d\omega_2 + \delta \omega_3 = 0
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi k
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi k
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta = \sum_{k} (-1)^k \partial_k^*
              is the alternating sum of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+a+differential+form"} pullbacks
              along the face maps of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi X
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}_\bullet
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Xu"}> Xu, def. 2.1
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#LGX"} LG-Xu, def. 2.1
            %strong twisted presymplectic groupoid
            in (
            %a{:href => "#BCWZ"}> BCWZ, def. 2.1
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Since therefore a (pre-)symplectic groupoid is really a Lie groupoid equipped with a cocycle in degree-3
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
              (instead of degree 2 as for a symplectic manifold), it is really rather an object in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-plectic+geometry"} 2-plectic geometry
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#lie_integration_and_poisson_manifolds Lie integration and Poisson manifolds
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} integrating
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+algebroid"} Poisson Lie algebroid
            is naturally a symplectic Lie groupoid. Picking always the unique source-simply connected integrating
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            produces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo :
                  %mi PoissonManifolds
                  %mo →
                  %mi SymplecticGroupoids
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Sigma : PoissonManifolds \to SymplecticGroupoids
                  \\,.
          %p
            When the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifold"} Poisson manifold
            we start with happens to be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi symplectic
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi iso
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (X,\pi)\;\; symplectic
                  \\;\;\Rightarrow\;\;
                  \\Sigma(X,\pi) \simeq_{iso} \Pi(X)
                  \\,.
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiscrete+category"} codiscrete groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Pair
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pair(X)
            we have that the symplectic form on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mor(\Pi(X)) = X \times X
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \otimes (-\omega)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic form
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Conversely, for every symplectic groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}
            there is a unique
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifold"} Poisson manifold
            structure on its manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}_0
            of objects such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
            map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \colon \mathbf{X}_1 \to \mathbf{X}_0
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifolds"} Poisson manifolds
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Racaniere"} Racaniere, theorem 6.3
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}
            %strong integrates the Poisson manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}_0
          %h3#symplectic_realization Symplectic realization
          %p
            The source map of a symplectic groupoid over a Poisson manifold constitutes a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+realization"} symplectic realization
            of this Poisson manifold, hence its canonical desingularization via
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+realization"} symplectic realization
            for more.
          %h3#in_geometric_quantization_of_poisson_manifolds In geometric quantization of Poisson manifolds
          %p
            In the
            %em groupoid approach to quantization
            symplectic groupoids are used to discuss
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            not just of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifold"} Poisson manifold
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization+of+symplectic+groupoids"} geometric quantization of symplectic groupoids
          %h3#as_lie_integration_of_poisson_lie_algebroid As Lie integration of Poisson Lie algebroid
          %p (…)
          %h3#a_reduced_phase_space_of_open_poisson_sigmamodel A reduced phase space of open Poisson sigma-model
          %p
            The symplectic groupoid of a Poisson manifold is also the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+phase+space"} reduced phase space
            of the open sector of the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+sigma-model"} Poisson sigma-model
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#CattaneoFelder01"} Cattaneo-Felder 01
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#OfLiePoissonStructure Of Lie-Poisson structure
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              and consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+vector+space"} dual vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^*
              equipped with its
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-Poisson+structure"} Lie-Poisson structure
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⫽
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^* \sslash G
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coadjoint+action"} coadjoint action
              carries a multiplicative symplectic form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              induced by the identification of the manifold of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+bundle"} cotangent bundle
              of the group,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo *
                      %mo ≃
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mo *
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \times \mathfrak{g}^* \simeq T^* G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincare+form"} Poincare form
              on the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+bundle"} cotangent bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{g}^* //G, \omega)
              a symplectic groupoid which
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integrates
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-Poisson+structure"} Lie-Poisson structure
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^*
          %p
            This seems to be due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Weinstein91"} Weinstein 1991, ex. 3.2
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BursztynCrainic"} Bursztyn &amp; Crainic 2005, ex. 4.3
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Nuiten13"} Nuiten 2013, p. 111
