            %p
              (adapted from
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Some+title+containing+the+words+%22homotopy%22+and+%22symplectic%22%2C+e.g.+this+one"} Ševera 00
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The notion of symplectic groupoids was apparently proposed independently by Karasëv,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"} Weinstein
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
          %ul
            %li#Weinstein87
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"}> Alan Weinstein
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Symplectic groupoids and Poisson manifolds
                %strong 16
                (1987) 101-104 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/bulletin-of-the-american-mathematical-society-new-series/volume-16/issue-1/Symplectic-groupoids-and-Poisson-manifolds/bams/1183553676.full"}> euclid:bams/1183553676
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"}> Alan Weinstein
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Symplectic groupoids, geometric quantization, and irrational rotation algebras
              %p
                %em Symplectic geometry, groupoids, and integrable systems
                (Berkeley, CA, 1989), Springer (1991) 281-290 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4613-9719-9_19"}> doi:10.1007/978-1-4613-9719-9_19
                , MR1104934&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"}> Alan Weinstein
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Tangential deformation quantization and polarized symplectic groupoids
                %em Deformation theory and symplectic geometry
                (Ascona, 1996), 301-314, Kluwer (1997) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/9780792345251"}> ISBN:9780792345251
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1480730"} MR1480730
            %li
              %p
                M. V. Karas"ev,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Maslov quantization conditions in higher cohomology and analogs of notions developed in Lie theory for canonical fibre bundles of symplectic manifolds II
            %li
              %p S. Zakrzewski, Quantum and classical pseudogroups I, II, Commun. Math. Phys. 134 (1990)
          %p
            See also the references at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization+of+symplectic+groupoids"} geometric quantization of symplectic groupoids
            \.
          %p Lecture notes include
          %ul
            %li#Racaniere
              Sébastien Racanière,
              %em Lie algebroids, Lie groupoids and Poisson geometry
              (
              %a{:href => "http://empg.maths.ed.ac.uk/Activities/GCY/Racaniere.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            The notion of pre-quasi-symplectic groupoids is introduced and the intepretation of symplectic groupoids in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            is made fairly explicit in
          %ul
            %li#Xu
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ping+Xu"}> Ping Xu
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Momentum Maps and Morita Equivalence
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0307319"} arXiv:math/0307319
            %li#LGX
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Camille+Laurent-Gengoux"}> Camille Laurent-Gengoux
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ping+Xu"} Ping Xu
                %em Quantization of pre-quasi-symplectic groupoids and their Hamiltonian spaces
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Breadth of Symplectic and Poisson Geometry
                %strong 232
                (2005) 423-454 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0311154"}> arXiv:math/0311154
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/0-8176-4419-9_14"} doi:10.1007/0-8176-4419-9_14
          %p These “pre-quasi-symplectic groupoids” had been called “twisted presymplectic groupoids” in
          %ul
            %li#BCWZ
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henrique+Bursztyn"}> Henrique Bursztyn
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marius+Crainic"} Marius Crainic
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"} Alan Weinstein
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chenchang+Zhu"} Chenchang Zhu
              %em Integration of twisted Dirac brackets
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0303180"}> arXiv:math/0303180
              )
          %p The identification with reduced phase spaces of the open Poisson sigma-model is in
          %ul
            %li#CattaneoFelder01
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Cattaneo"}> Alberto Cattaneo
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Felder"} Giovanni Felder
              = succeed "," do
                %em Poisson sigma models and symplectic groupoids
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantization of Singular Symplectic Quotients
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaas+Landsman"} Klaas Landsman
              %p
                2001), 61–93. (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0003023"}> arXiv:math/0003023
                )
          %p Further developments:
          %ul
            %li#Weinstein91
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"}> Alan Weinstein
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Noncommutative geometry and geometric quantization
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Symplectic geometry and Mathematical physics
                %strong 99
                Birkhäuser (1991) 446-461.
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4757-2140-9_23"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-2140-9_23
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ping+Xu"}> Ping Xu
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Morita equivalence and symplectic realizations of Poisson manifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=ASENS_1992_4_25_3_307_0"} NUMDAM
            %li#BursztynCrainic
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henrique+Bursztyn"}> Henrique Bursztyn
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marius+Crainic"} Marius Crainic
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dirac structures, momentum maps and quasi-Poisson manifolds
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Breadth of Symplectic and Poisson Geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 232
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/0-8176-4419-9_1"} doi:10.1007/0-8176-4419-9_1
            %li
              %p
                F. Bonechi, N. Ciccoli, N. Staffolani, M. Tarlini,
                %em The quantization of the symplectic groupoid of the standard Podles sphere
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1004.3163"}> arXiv:1004.3163
                )
            %li#Nuiten13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joost+Nuiten"}> Joost Nuiten
                , pp. 108 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/master+thesis+Nuiten"} Cohomological quantization of local prequantum boundary field theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "/schreiber/files/thesisNuiten.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://dspace.library.uu.nl/handle/1874/282756"} dspace:1874/282756
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "/schreiber/files/thesisNuitenTalk.pdf"} talk slides
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+groupoid"} formal groupoid
            version of symplectic groupoids is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+S.+Cattaneo"}> Alberto Cattaneo
              , Benoit Dherin,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Felder"} Giovanni Felder
              = succeed "," do
                %em Formal symplectic groupoid
              %strong 253
              (2005), no. 3, 645–674
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0312380"} math.SG/0312380
              = succeed ";" do
                %a#CattaneoDherinFelder{:href => "HTTP://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s00220-004-1199-z"} doi
              = succeed "," do
                %em Formal Lagrangian operad
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0505051"} math.SG/0505051
